For every number:

-->1.Add it to the current sum.
-->2.Update the maximum sum if needed.
-->3.If the current sum becomes negative, reset it to 0.


code:
nums = [-2,1,-3,4,-1,2,1,-5,4]
current_sum=0
max_sum=float('-inf')
for num in nums:
    current_sum+=num
    max_sum=max(current_sum,max_sum)
    if current_sum<0:
        current_sum=0

print(max_sum)


-->Think of current_sum as your "score."

If your score is positive, it can help future numbers make an even bigger sum, so keep it.
If your score is negative, it will only reduce any future sum, so discard it and start fresh.

That's exactly why Kadane's algorithm is both correct and efficient.


Time Complexity: O(n) (one pass through the array)
Space Complexity: O(1) (only two variables are used)
